<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Renim AI collects, uses and protects your information.">
  <!-- Template — have this reviewed by a lawyer before launch. Replace [COMPANY LEGAL NAME], [COMPANY ADDRESS], [CONTACT EMAIL] and [EFFECTIVE DATE]. -->
  <p class="meta">Last updated: [EFFECTIVE DATE]</p>
  <p class="box">In short: we collect what we need to run Renim AI for you, we don’t sell your data, and you can export your data or delete your account at any time from Profile.</p>

  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how [COMPANY LEGAL NAME] (“we”, “us”) collects, uses and shares information when you use Renim AI, including our web app and Chrome extension (the “Service”).</p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Account information</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, email address and password. Passwords are stored only as a salted hash, never in plain text.</li>
    <li>Optional security settings such as two-factor authentication, and your organization, team and role information.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Content you create or upload</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Meeting audio recordings, transcripts, summaries, notes, tasks, calendar events, documents and files you upload, and your conversations with the AI assistant.</li>
    <li>This content is stored in our PostgreSQL database and linked to your account.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Chrome extension</h3>
  <p>If you install our Chrome extension, it captures the live captions of a Google Meet call <strong>only after you start it</strong> for that meeting, and sends them to your Renim AI account. It does not capture anything from meetings you have not started it for. You are responsible for telling other participants and getting any consent required where you live.</p>
  <h3>Billing information</h3>
  <p>Payments are handled by our payment processors (Razorpay and/or Stripe). We receive your plan, payment status and limited transaction details. We do not store full card numbers.</p>
  <h3>Technical information</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Basic logs such as IP address, browser type and timestamps, used for security, rate limiting, debugging and audit trails.</li>
    <li>If error monitoring is enabled, technical error reports (not your meeting content) may be sent to our error-monitoring provider.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the Service: transcribing meetings, generating summaries, action items and briefings, and keeping your notes, tasks and calendar in sync.</li>
    <li>To secure accounts, prevent abuse and keep audit logs.</li>
    <li>To process payments and manage subscriptions.</li>
    <li>To send service emails such as password resets, invitations and important account notices.</li>
    <li>To fix bugs and improve reliability.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use your content to train our own AI models.</p>

  <h2>3. AI processing</h2>
  <p>To produce transcripts, summaries and answers, the relevant content (for example a transcript or note) is sent to the AI model provider configured for the Service. If you or your organization set up your own AI provider or API key, your content is sent to that provider under its own terms. We send only what is needed for the request you made.</p>

  <h2>4. Who we share information with</h2>
  <p>We share information only with service providers that help us run the Service, under agreements that limit how they can use it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Hosting and database providers, to store your account and content.</li>
    <li>AI model providers, to process your requests as described above.</li>
    <li>Payment processors (Razorpay, Stripe).</li>
    <li>Email delivery (Resend), when email is enabled.</li>
    <li>Error monitoring (Sentry), when enabled.</li>
    <li>Integrations you choose to connect (for example Slack, Microsoft Teams, Jira, GitHub or webhooks). We send data to them only when you tell us to.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>In an organization workspace, other members can see content shared with that workspace according to their role. We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect the rights and safety of our users and the public.</p>

  <h2>5. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>We use your browser’s local storage and essential cookies to keep you signed in and remember your preferences. We do not use advertising cookies or third-party ad trackers.</p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>We keep your account and content while your account is active. When you delete your account, we delete your personal data and content from our active systems, except limited records we must keep by law (for example billing records). Backups are overwritten on a rolling basis.</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights and choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access and export:</strong> download a copy of your data from <em>Profile</em> in the app.</li>
    <li><strong>Correction:</strong> update your details in <em>Profile</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> delete your account from <em>Profile</em>, or contact us.</li>
    <li>Depending on where you live, you may have more rights (for example to object to or restrict processing, or to complain to a data protection authority). Email [CONTACT EMAIL] to use them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>We use encryption in transit (HTTPS), hashed passwords, optional two-factor authentication, role-based access controls and audit logs. No system is perfectly secure, so please use a strong, unique password.</p>

  <h2>9. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Our providers may process data in countries other than yours. Where required, we use appropriate safeguards for these transfers.</p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>The Service is not meant for children under 16 (or the minimum age in your country), and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. If we make significant changes, we will let you know by email or in the app before they take effect.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>[COMPANY LEGAL NAME], [COMPANY ADDRESS]. Email: <a href="mailto:[CONTACT EMAIL]">[CONTACT EMAIL]</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
